From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nouveau: avoid legacy VGA CRTC locking on headless GF117

GF117 has no display heads. Generic devinit preinit/dtor call lockvgac,
whose initial rdvgac writes CRTC index 0x1f to 0x6013d4. The notebook's
stock driver reports a PRIVRING fault at that address during both load
and removal. Avoid all accesses in this lock helper on chipset 0xd7.
Keep the behavior on other Fermi, Kepler and legacy chips unchanged.

Hardware reference: envytools/docs/hw/gpu.rst (GF117, HEADs column).
This source correction still requires physical validation on the notebook.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/disp/vga.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/disp/vga.c
@@ -127,8 +127,15 @@
 bool
 nvkm_lockvgac(struct nvkm_device *device, bool lock)
 {
-	bool locked = !nvkm_rdvgac(device, 0, 0x1f);
+	bool locked;
 	u8 data = lock ? 0x99 : 0x57;
+
+	/* GF117 is a render-only Optimus GPU without display heads. Legacy
+	 * VGA CRTC accesses fault, including the index write in rdvgac(). */
+	if (device->chipset == 0xd7)
+		return false;
+
+	locked = !nvkm_rdvgac(device, 0, 0x1f);
 	if (device->card_type < NV_50)
 		nvkm_wrvgac(device, 0, 0x1f, data);
 	else
